I am from Grand Rapids Michigan so not  too far from Hillsdale so in high school  I played football hockey and lacrosse  loved all three so I wasn't even sure in  high school that I wanted to pursue  football I guess more more than the  other sports it pursued me I've got a  great relationship with Coach Otterbein  kids during my time there and I believe  it's still the case today but he's the  running backs coach so as a running back  I spent a lot of time with Coach  Otterbein he knows a lot about football  he's had a lot of success at Hillsdale  College on top of that you know he holds  a Bible study every Friday morning in  his office that aspect of things really  drew me in I think part of the the fun  of being at Hillsdale is it was such a  small school and we were able to compete  with the larger schools and that was  something that we always cherished and  kind of had the chip on our shoulder to  knock off the you know the David versus  Goliath type it was a hard-working Bunch  the culture was definitely one of  winning when I came in there that tide  was turning a guest for Hillsdale  College my freshman year we made the  playoffs sophomore year we made the  playoffs junior year we didn't make the  playoffs but we actually won the GLIAC  which is you know funny how that works  it was a winning culture it was  competitive hard-working and that's both  on the field in the classroom success of  a running back depends on everyone else  essentially so I was fortunate enough to  play with great offensive lineman I was  fortunate to play with great  quarterbacks great receivers so you know  having all those other weapons at your  disposal on offense really opens things  up for running back the memory that  would stand out most to me from my time  at Hillsdale College was my junior year  when we were able to win the GLIAC  Conference championship to my knowledge  that hadn't been done in quite some time  we won the GLIAC on Saturday then we had  our team banquet on Sunday and remember  coach out of mind getting up to the  podium and just screaming in joy because  it was such a great accomplishment  something we were all very proud of  relatively quickly after graduation I  became engaged to my now wife Katie  Katie was my girlfriend junior and  senior year at Hillsdale College and she  was a loyal fan she would drive up from  Indiana University come to a few  a year I have a daughter that is six  months old which has been a game changer  in a good way our lives will never be  the same but we don't ever want it to be  the same because she's been such a  blessing to us we enjoy everyday with  her it's something new something  exciting for sure I guess a byproduct of  being on a great team is that individual  awards or induction such as this come  about so I'm humbled that I was one that  was chosen  [Music]
 

